.el .ds Aq '
.TH netmeter 1  "netmeter 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
netmeter \- Local\-first LAN/WAN/TOTAL bandwidth meter (Linux)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnetmeter\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Local\-first LAN/WAN/TOTAL bandwidth meter (Linux)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
netmeter\-live(1)
Live 1s dashboard (q to quit)
.TP
netmeter\-show(1)
Show historical usage
.TP
netmeter\-top(1)
Top talkers by iface or day
.TP
netmeter\-status(1)
Daemon + system status
.TP
netmeter\-config(1)
Config get/set/path/reset
.TP
netmeter\-export(1)
Export range to csv/json
.TP
netmeter\-import(1)
One\-shot vnStat history import (vnstat \-\-json)
.TP
netmeter\-completions(1)
Shell completions
.TP
netmeter\-manpage(1)
Print roff man page to stdout (packaging embeds it)
.TP
netmeter\-daemon(1)
Background daemon controls
.TP
netmeter\-user\-agent(1)
Per\-user budget notifier (runs as systemd \-\-user unit)
.TP
netmeter\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
